WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:12.420
- If we talk about our
traditional architecture

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.160
here in Senegal, we cannot not talk about

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.750
earth architecture because
everything was built with earth,

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.153
and during the industrialisation,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:28.990
the colonists made us think
that concrete was better,

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.580
that it was faster.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.340
I really want to prove people
that earth architecture

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.993
can be as modern, as circular you know...

00:00:37.991 --> 00:00:39.260
It could fix a lot of problems.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.920
- What's really interesting
is the new technologies

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.860
that we have can really push that material

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.710
to a different place.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:50.720
That becomes a really
interesting narrative

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.740
of an existing historical material

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.120
becoming a future material.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.550
- I think it's the job
of every architect now

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.240
here in Senegal, all the young architects,

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.570
to promote this material.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:04.870
- And it's contextual.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.580
It's a material that's found
in a place, it's abundant.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.290
That's why it was built with before.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:12.400
I'm creating a contextual
materials library for Johannesburg

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.610
a materials archive of what's
happening in Johannesburg

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:19.710
within a circular design context.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.230
The whole intention is then

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:24.680
to bring Johannesburg-based
designers into a space

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.820
to communicate about the
material makeup of Johannesburg,

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.360
and therefore, we start

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.420
to create this really, really,
really interesting archive

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.990
where people are become
a part of the movement,

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.520
they become emotionally
invested in these materials

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.187
because we're talking about
them, what do they mean to you?

